If you are staying in Sharm El Sheikh and want to experience the natural beauty of Sinai, a day trip to Ras Mohammed National Park and Magic Lake is an excellent choice.

## Explore Ras Mohammed National Park

Ras Mohammed is famous for its spectacular Red Sea coastline, colorful coral reefs, and unique desert landscapes. During the trip, visitors can explore some of the area's most impressive natural attractions.

The snorkeling stop at Coral Gardens offers an opportunity to discover colorful fish and beautiful underwater scenery in the clear Red Sea waters.

## Visit the Gate of Allah

One of the most recognizable photo stops is the famous Gate of Allah. Surrounded by the dramatic Sinai desert, it is a great place to stop, take photos, and enjoy the scenery.

## Discover the Mangrove Channel

The tour also takes you to the Mangrove Channel, where mangrove trees grow directly in the salty waters of the Red Sea. This unusual environment adds another interesting side to the Ras Mohammed experience.

## See the Earthquake Crack

Another fascinating stop is the ancient Earthquake Crack, a dramatic geological formation created by movements beneath the earth thousands of years ago.

## Swim at Magic Lake

The adventure continues at Magic Lake, known for its beautiful blue water and peaceful desert surroundings. Take a swim, relax beside the lake, and enjoy one of Sinai's most memorable natural landscapes.

